## Module 14 — Cost Management
**Oracle Equivalent:** Oracle Fusion Cost Management

### NexusAI Pages Currently Existing
- ✅ [StandardCosting.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/StandardCosting.tsx) (8.4KB)
- ✅ [CostInsights.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/CostInsights.tsx) (6.4KB)
- ✅ [CostingProfitability.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/CostingProfitability.tsx)
- ✅ `cost-management/` sub-directory — 5 pages
- ✅ Schema: [costing.ts](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/shared/schema/costing.ts) with standard costs, overhead rules, cost elements

### Oracle Pages/Forms NexusAI is Missing or Partial
| Oracle Form | NexusAI Status | Gap Description |
|---|---|---|
| **Cost Processor (Background Worker)** | ❌ Missing | Oracle's async cost processor intercepts every inventory transaction and values it using the configured cost method. No automation exists in Nexus. |
| **Cost Rollup Engine** | ❌ Missing | Multi-level BOM traversal that rolls up material + labor + overhead costs to compute the standard cost of a finished good. |
| **Receipt Accounting (AP Accruals)** | ❌ Missing | Oracle auto-posts "Inventory AP Accruals" when a PO receipt occurs, and clears on invoice match. This bridge between PO/INV/AP doesn't exist in Nexus. |
| **Average / FIFO / LIFO Cost Methods** | ❌ Missing | Nexus supports Standard Costing. Oracle also supports Average, FIFO, LIFO with separate cost layer tracking. |
| **Periodic Average Costing** | ❌ Missing | Calculating average costs at month-end across all receipts in the period. |
| **Cost Group Setup** | ❌ Missing | Different cost methods per inventory organization. |
| **Cost Comparison Report** | ⚠️ Partial | Cost Insights exists as a manual report. Missing: Automated variance roll: actual vs. standard by cost element. |

